[h1]OpenZone Trader for VPP Admin Tools[/h1]
The trader's module in the OpenZone window of VPP Admin Tools: eight pages on the window's rail, in English and Ukrainian.
[list]
[*][b]Points[/b]: every trader, a character or an object. Place one where you stand, turn it to face you, dress a character as you are dressed; its categories, price factors, money and who may trade with it.
[*][b]Goods[/b]: categories and their lines, prices, parts and stock rules.
[*][b]Conditions and discounts[/b]: who sees a line and for how much, from any mod that answers; a research node is picked on its tree (with OpenZone Trader Research).
[*][b]Stock[/b], [b]Licences[/b], [b]Money[/b]: the shelves and their lines, the licences and who holds them, the notes, condition factors and the rules of a deal.
[*][b]TraderPlus import[/b]: a dry run with a report of what comes over and what is left out, then the apply on one confirmation.
[*][b]Config files[/b]: the trader's three files as text, checked before they are written.
[/list]
Edits gather in a draft, are checked, and go to the server together; the server reloads the trader at once.

[b]Needs[/b] OpenZone Trader, OpenZone Core, the OpenZone tab for VPP Admin Tools and VPPAdminTools. Admin rights are VPP's own (the permission OpenZone:Admin).

Source: github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-trader. Licence: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the series' NOTICE.

